From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 11:10:47 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] HID: apple-mtp-haptic: check the mode-switch report only on
 SPI actuators

"HID: spi-hid-apple: stop status mismatches on boot and suspend" skips
feature report 0x21 when the actuator's descriptor does not declare it,
as on the J313 SPI actuator, and then
reports success for both modes. Two problems follow on our machines.

The MTP actuators of the M2, M4 Pro and MacBook Neo take report 0x21
because their firmware does, not because a descriptor lists it, and
nothing shows that their descriptors do. If one does not, the check
would silently stop the probe from putting a warm-rebooted actuator
back in device-controlled mode, and stop host-controlled click feedback,
on hardware where both work today. Apply the check to SPI actuators
only, where the descriptor was read.

A request for host-controlled mode that cannot be sent is not a
success. hid-magicmouse falls back to the firmware's click when the
switch fails; reporting success instead makes it believe it drives the
actuator while the firmware still does. Return -EOPNOTSUPP for it, and
keep returning 0 for device-controlled mode, which the part is in from
power-up.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
---
 drivers/hid/hid-apple-mtp-haptic.c | 10 +++++++---
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/hid/hid-apple-mtp-haptic.c b/drivers/hid/hid-apple-mtp-haptic.c
index 578afd24ef..aa1e02e1f6 100644
--- a/drivers/hid/hid-apple-mtp-haptic.c
+++ b/drivers/hid/hid-apple-mtp-haptic.c
@@ -62,11 +62,15 @@ int apple_taptic_switch_modes(struct hid_device *haptic_hdev, bool enable_host_c
 	 * Sending 0x21 makes the controller return status 9c 17 e5 f8
 	 * instead of the write-ok status. The part powers up
 	 * device-controlled, which is what a false argument asks for.
-	 * A true argument has no 0x21 report to send either.
+	 * Host control cannot be taken without the report, so refuse it
+	 * and let the caller keep the firmware's click. The MTP actuators
+	 * take 0x21 whatever their descriptor says, so only an SPI one
+	 * is checked.
 	 */
-	if (!apple_taptic_has_report(haptic_hdev, HID_FEATURE_REPORT, 0x21) &&
+	if (haptic_hdev->bus == BUS_SPI &&
+	    !apple_taptic_has_report(haptic_hdev, HID_FEATURE_REPORT, 0x21) &&
 	    !apple_taptic_has_report(haptic_hdev, HID_OUTPUT_REPORT, 0x21))
-		return 0;
+		return enable_host_controlled ? -EOPNOTSUPP : 0;
 
 	ret = hid_hw_raw_request(haptic_hdev, msg[0], msg, sizeof(msg),
 				 HID_FEATURE_REPORT, HID_REQ_SET_REPORT);
